As a troop-contributing country that supports the United Nations in the search 
for peace, Burkina Faso has, despite its own internal situation, deployed 1,130 troops, 
including one battalion and two formed police units and 60 individual posts.

Turning now to peace and stability in the Southern African region, I note that 
while it remains relatively stable, there is an emerging threat to peace and security, 
due to increasing acts of terrorism and insurgency.
